      "totalDuration": "8 yrs",
      "description": "• Led the end-to-end rebuild of publishing infrastructure across multiple Block Communications organizations, replacing ad-hoc, cron-driven workflows with an event-driven platform orchestrated via RabbitMQ and Kubernetes. Achieved zero-downtime regional cutovers and cut publish latency from ~60 s to ~5 s while adding real-time observability across 30+ custom microservices.\n\n• Engineered a geo-distributed web platform on Kubernetes, leveraging NGINX Ingress and Varnish caching to serve 2–3 million monthly requests with sub-100 ms latency and zero platform-level downtime.\n\n• Engineered RESTful APIs and webhooks integrating external vendor systems for identity, subscription, and payment workflows. Implemented Google OAuth login and a public content API enabling secure third-party access.\n\n• Built and maintained a single-node Hadoop/HBase data platform (32 GB RAM) supporting content discovery, personalization, and analytics workloads for both logged-in and anonymous users. Optimized performance to sustain high-volume queries and recommendations for 8+ years on minimal hardware.\n\n• Partnered with newsroom, development, and operations teams to translate time-sensitive editorial and business requirements into scalable API designs, infrastructure updates, and automated deployment strategies, improving delivery turnaround by ~30%.\n\n• Developed and maintained CI/CD pipelines using Jenkins and Kubernetes to automate testing and deployment for 30+ custom microservices, increasing release frequency and stability, and eliminating reliance on third-party deployment tooling.",
